MATLAB is optional for inspecting or visualizing an approved CSV fixture; it is not a stated assignment requirement. Python and repository-controlled tools remain authoritative for validation, dispatch, scoring, and results.

## Small MATLAB read-and-plot test

Use only a public or instructor-approved fixture. The supplied sources do not provide a fixture filename, so replace the placeholder with the confirmed local path. This reads the current seven-column site-level CSV contract and plots two capacity fields; it assumes no coordinates, MAT-file, solver, or MATLAB-specific schema.

~~~matlab
fixturePath = "path/to/public_or_instructor_approved_fixture.csv";
T = readtable(fixturePath, "VariableNamingRule", "preserve");
required = ["team_id", "site_id", "bus_id", ...
    "connection_capacity_mw", "generator_capacity_mw", ...
    "storage_power_mw", "storage_energy_mwh"];
missing = setdiff(required, string(T.Properties.VariableNames));
assert(isempty(missing), ...
    "Missing required CSV field(s): %s", strjoin(missing, ", "));
assert(isequal(string(T.Properties.VariableNames), required), ...
    "CSV headers must match the seven-column canonical contract exactly and in order.");
x = T{:, "connection_capacity_mw"};
y = T{:, "generator_capacity_mw"};
assert(isnumeric(x) && isnumeric(y), "Plotted capacity columns must be numeric.");
assert(all(isfinite(x)) && all(isfinite(y)), "Plotted capacity columns must contain finite values.");
figure; scatter(x, y, 36, "filled");
xlabel("Connection capacity (MW)"); ylabel("Generator capacity (MW)");
title("Approved CSV fixture: site capacities"); grid on;
~~~

A passing test shows only that this approved fixture can be read and visualized; it does not reproduce an ACTIVSg2000 scenario, dispatch, score, or solver result.

